From: Takoserver Native source candidate
Subject: [SOURCE ONLY v6.12] wait matched NF readers before original namespace reference put

Apply after the retained aggregate17. The direct RELEASE_NAMESPACE operation
already irreversibly cuts admission and seals its original counters. Match
CUT's synchronize_net after unlocking, before clearing the original context
and putting its one net reference. Only the successful first release waits.
This joins the existing matched NF reader interval only, never all task,
packet/queue/okfn/GRO/offload lifetime or terminal/readiness authority.
Existing net_free final callback and all admission/ownership APIs stay intact.

diff --git a/net/core/tako_terminal.c b/net/core/tako_terminal.c
--- a/net/core/tako_terminal.c
+++ b/net/core/tako_terminal.c
@@ -445,6 +445,12 @@
 	tako_terminal_state_seal(&owner->state);
 	tako_terminal_state_seal(&owner->device_associations);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&owner->lock, flags);
+
+	/* Direct RELEASE_NAMESPACE must wait the same pre-gate NF reader
+	 * sections as CUT before dropping this original net reference.
+	 * This does not join okfn/queued/GRO/offload continuations.
+	 */
+	synchronize_net();
 	/* Clear the original context BEFORE the one raw put, never adopt or
 	 * drop another FD/PID's namespace. File ref keeps owner independently.
 	 */
